    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="contextory-v0-6-0" tabindex="-1">Contextory v0.6.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#contextory-v0-6-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contextory v0.6.0&quot;">\u200B</a></h1><p>Keep each project in a multi-folder workspace separate, coordinate requests across selected projects, and let existing native MCP connections recover from delayed Contextory startup.</p><h2 id="changes" tabindex="-1">Changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Changes&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><ul><li>Add a <strong>Project</strong> selector and project badges on requests and specs. Each folder keeps its own requests, symbols, knowledge, history, versions, checks, sessions and evidence. Duplicate folder names remain distinguishable.</li><li>Select affected projects in <strong>New request</strong> to create linked local request branches. Open each branch from <strong>Across projects</strong>. The aggregate completes only after every local branch completes; missing, offline or removed projects keep it incomplete.</li><li>Retain the original request input for explicit, idempotent recovery after partial creation. Each branch keeps its own milestones, specs, lease and verification; creation is recoverable rather than atomic across repositories.</li><li>Scope native tools with <code>projectId</code> and, when needed, <code>workspaceId</code>. An omitted/current project always means that native server&#39;s own project, regardless of UI selection or earlier calls. Peer routing verifies identity and preserves native roles. Read-only <code>codebaseId</code> references remain separate from writable workspace members.</li><li>Add <code>contextory_workspace_get</code>, <code>contextory_workspace_request_create</code>, CLI <code>projects [group-id]</code> and <code>--project</code>/<code>--workspace</code> flags. Update shared instructions and portable skills.</li><li>Use folder-specific startup preferences, checks and source navigation. Cursor traces and unsaved overlays follow the actual source folder. Removing and re-adding a folder preserves its existing storage and records.</li><li>Clear project-specific UI state on switching and reject delayed replies, including old dashboard restores after the new project has loaded.</li><li>Keep MCP discovery available while a managed native proxy retries delayed service readiness in the background for up to <strong>five minutes</strong>. Each foreground readiness wait stays bounded to fifteen seconds. Mutations are dispatched once and are never automatically replayed.</li></ul><p>See the <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/compare/v0.5.1...v0.6.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">commit comparison</a>, <a href="./../USER-GUIDE.html#multiple-projects-in-one-workspace">multi-project guide</a> and <a href="./../USER-GUIDE.html#resume-an-existing-chat">connection recovery</a>.</p><h2 id="install-or-upgrade" tabindex="-1">Install or upgrade <a class="header-anchor" href="#install-or-upgrade" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Install or upgrade&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><ol><li>Use Windows, Node.js <strong>24+</strong>, and VS Code <strong>1.96+</strong> or IBM Bob. Open a trusted local folder or a workspace with separate, non-nested project folders.</li><li>Download <code>contextory-workspace-0.6.0.vsix</code> and <code>contextory-workspace-0.6.0.sha256</code> from the <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/releases/tag/v0.6.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub release</a>. Compare the VSIX SHA-256 with the checksum file.</li><li>Choose <strong>Extensions &gt; Install from VSIX</strong>, select the package and reload when prompted. VS Code users can run <code>code --install-extension .\\contextory-workspace-0.6.0.vsix</code>.</li><li>After the managed tool catalog changes, use <strong>Contextory: Restart Agent Extensions</strong> or the native client&#39;s MCP reload control. Resume/reopen an older chat if it still advertises the previous tools. Native project and hook trust remain client-owned.</li><li>Choose the intended project in Contextory. In native chat, ask the agent to discover workspace membership and carry explicit project scope through related operations.</li></ol><p>Existing single-folder records and client configuration are preserved. Removing a workspace folder does not delete its records. The five-minute readiness recovery handles an already-configured native connection starting before the service; it does not approve hooks or force every existing chat to discover new tools.</p><h2 id="validation-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Validation and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#validation-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Validation and limits&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Qualification includes <strong>97 backend tests</strong>, <strong>35 UI tests</strong>, typechecking, native/headless transport and registration checks, portable-resource validation and the complete documentation build. The extracted package is exercised in disposable VS Code and IBM Bob profiles with two project folders. See the <a href="./../VALIDATION.html">validation record</a>.</p><p>Up to sixteen separate local project roots are accepted. Nested/remote roots, other operating systems, authenticated native-agent conversations and large-workspace performance remain unqualified. Static diagrams show possible bounded paths. Each cross-project branch requires independent local completion; there is no shared lease or atomic repository-wide transaction. Distribution uses GitHub release assets; the project remains <strong>UNLICENSED</strong>.</p>', 11)
